scripts/.osm-ingest-progress.json

# Phoenix venue-count working data (count-only scope; Places place_id+coords only, never ingested)
/phoenix-count/

# Reno-Sparks merged research artifacts (input to scripts/import-reno-merged.mjs). Untracked for the
# same reason as phoenix-count: research working data, and it carries tier-4 aggregator source URLs
# which are a private research input under ADR-14 and must never be republished.
/reno-count/

# Daytona/Volusia research artifacts (input to scripts/import-daytona-merged.mjs). Same rationale as
# reno-count: research working data carrying tier-4 aggregator source URLs (ADR-14 private input).
/daytona-count/

# Greensboro-High Point research artifacts (input to scripts/import-greensboro-merged.mjs). Same
# rationale: research working data, and the workbook's held-back candidate set is sourced partly to
# playtimescheduler.com — a tier-4 aggregator, ADR-14 private research input, never republished.
/greensboro-count/

# Little Rock MSA research artifacts (input to scripts/import-little-rock-merged.mjs). Same rationale:
# research working data, and the workbook's held-back candidate set cites openstreetmap.org and
# mysaline.com only on several rows (tier-4 / secondary, ADR-14 private input, never republished).
/little-rock-count/

# Google Places match proposals from scripts/backfill-place-ids.mjs (--dry-run output, hand-reviewed
# before --apply). Holds Places displayName/location used only to validate a match in memory; ADR-12
# permits storing place_id alone, so this working file stays out of the repo.
/place-id-backfill/

# Generic metro-research pipeline artifacts (input to scripts/import-metro-merged.mjs, produced by
# scripts/lib/workbook-extract.mjs). Same rationale as the per-metro dirs above: research working
# data, and the workbooks carry tier-4 aggregator source URLs which are an ADR-14 private research
# input and must never be republished. Also holds the shared Nominatim geocode cache.
/metro-research/

# Nominatim geocode cache, if one is ever written at the repo root. Nothing should write here any
# more — scripts/lib/geocode-nominatim.mjs defaults inside metro-research/ as of 2026-08-04 — so this
# is a backstop for a stray --cache argument or a script that predates that change.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TREATING IT AS PROTECTION. An ignore entry does NOT save a directory from
# `git clean -fdx`: `-x` removes ignored files too, and that is exactly what destroyed the geocode
# cache on 2026-08-03. What it does buy is real but narrower — the path was previously untracked AND
# unignored, which meant a plain `git clean -fd` reached it and a `git add -A` would have staged
# ~1 MB of churning research data into the public repo. The actual protection for the cache is its
# LOCATION (metro-research/ is a junction to a repo outside every working tree, which git clean
# provably does not follow), not this line.
/.geocode-cache/

# Link-health sweep artifacts (scripts/link-health-sweep.mjs). Run output, not source: each sweep
# writes a timestamped JSON of every URL probed plus its verdict. Same posture as the metro research
# artifacts above — the SCRIPT is tracked, the run output is not. See the caveat on /.geocode-cache/
# about what an ignore entry does and does not protect against.
/link-health/
